.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
.TH NFC-WRITE-NDEF 1 "2026-06-27" "libnci 1.0.0-alpha.1" "libnci manual"
.SH NAME
nfc-write-ndef \- write an NDEF message to a Type 4 tag
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nfc-write-ndef
.RB ( --uri
.IR URI " | "
.B --text
.IR TEXT " [" --lang " " LL "] | "
.BR --format )
.RI [ --read-only "] [" options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nfc-write-ndef
builds a URI or Text NDEF record (or prepares an empty message), waits for a
writable NFC Forum Type 4 tag and writes it. The write order is NLEN=0, then
the message, then NLEN, so a concurrent reader never observes a partial
message. After a successful write the message is read back and compared unless
.B --no-verify
is given. The operation is performed on the first suitable tag, then the tool
exits.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Content (choose one)
.TP
.BI --uri " URI"
Write a single URI record (common schemes are abbreviated per the NFC Forum
URI table).
.TP
.BI --text " TEXT"
Write a single UTF-8 Text record.
.TP
.BI --lang " LL"
IANA language code for
.BR --text " (default: " en ).
.TP
.B --format
Reset the tag to an empty NDEF message (NLEN=0).
.SS Modifiers
.TP
.B --read-only
Make the NDEF file read-only after any write (sets the CC write access to
0xFF). Irreversible on tags that lock the CC.
.TP
.B --no-verify
Skip the post-write read-back check.
.SS Device
.TP
.BI --chipset " NAME"
Controller driver to use.
.TP
.BI --bus " PATH" ", " --addr " HEX" ", " --chip " PATH"
I2C bus, controller address and GPIO chip.
.TP
.BI --ven " N" ", " --irq " N" ", " --dwl " N"
GPIO line offsets for VEN, IRQ and DWL.
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Print usage and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if the operation completed on a tag, non-zero on bad arguments, a device-open
failure, or a write/lock error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
nfc-write-ndef --uri https://qzx.is
nfc-write-ndef --text "hello world" --lang en
nfc-write-ndef --format
nfc-write-ndef --uri https://qzx.is --read-only
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nfc-read-ndef (1),
.BR nfc-poll (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Part of the libnci NFC stack.
